  - remaining useful life
  - reference capacity
  - end of life
  - censoring
  - benchmark reproducibility
  - preregistration
abstract: >-
  Code, processed data, frozen outputs and supplementary materials for a
  study of how the reference capacity used to define capacity-based state of
  health (nominal capacity or a measured early-cycle reference), the
  end-of-life threshold fraction and the endpoint rule change end-of-life
  labels, censoring, SOH benchmark errors and the conclusions of RUL method
  comparisons. Datasets: CALCE CS2 (quality-control development), XJTU (55
  NCM cells), HUST (77 LFP/graphite cells), MIT/Severson et al. (124
  LFP/graphite cells) and TJU (66 NCA and 55 NCM cells). Version 2.0.0 adds
  the MIT and TJU pipelines, the RUL method-comparison tests v1-v4 (protocols,
  amendments, reports and frozen outputs), the scripts and data behind
  Figures 1-6 and Supplementary Tables S1-S15, and Supplementary Notes S1-S4
  of the manuscript prepared for the Journal of Energy Storage. Version 1.0.0
  (doi:10.5281/zenodo.23889698) accompanied the IJPHM technical brief.
